  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let $R$ be the required relation\n$\\mathrm{A}=\\{(1,1)(2,2),(3,3)\\}$\n(i) $|\\mathrm{R}|=3$, when $\\mathrm{R}=\\mathrm{A}$\n(ii) $|\\mathrm{R}|=5$, e.g. $\\mathrm{R}=\\mathrm{A} \\cup\\{(1,2),(2,1)\\}$\n\nNumber of $R$ can be [3]\n(iii) $\\mathrm{R}=\\{1,2,3\\} \\times\\{1,2,3\\}$\nAns. (5)",
    "image": null
  },
